  "mpvCacheHelpDefaultContent": "Automatic. The player picks a suitable buffering strength based on the source type — more standard for local files, automatically steadier buffering for heavier network sources.",
  "mpvCacheHelpLowLatencyContent": "Lightest read-ahead with the fastest seeking, switching and refill, but the weakest jitter resistance. Best for local videos, or for a hands-on feel when the LAN is very stable.",
  "mpvCacheHelpStableContent": "Moderately heavy buffering that prioritizes reducing jitter-induced stutter. Seeking feels a bit slower than ultra-fast, but it suits most NAS, cloud drive and STRM viewing.",
  "mpvCacheHelpNetworkContent": "The heaviest tier, giving high-bitrate cloud drive, STRM and NAS sources more read-ahead room. Startup and refill after seeking are heavier, but it resists fluctuations best.",
